==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}} (abbreviated as [[AC]])
# an [[electric current]] in which the [[direction]] of [[flow]] of the [[electron]]s [[reverse]]s [[periodically]], such as sawtooth, sinusoidal or square wave current.
# an [[electric current]] in which the [[direction]] of [[flow]] of the [[electron]]s [[reverse]]s [[periodically]] by a sinusoidal law, hence having an average of zero, with positive and negative values (with a [[frequency]] of 50 Hz in Europe, 60 Hz in the US, 400 Hz for airport lighting, and some others); especially such a current produced by a [[rotating]] [[generator]] or [[alternator]].

